  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-notify",
      "text": "English | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\nA [DeepSeek Harness (DSH)](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) plugin that pushes key agent events to **DingTalk / WeCom (企业微信) / Feishu** group-bot webhooks — so you can close your laptop and still know the moment your agent finishes, errors, or waits for your approval."
    },
    {
      "section": "Events",
      "text": "| Event | Notification | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `agent/status` (running → idle) | ✅ Task finished | First-seen idle (e.g. right after boot) stays silent |\n| `agent/error` | ❌ Execution error (turn/step + error summary) | |\n| `approval/request` | ⚠️ Approval needed (tool + reason) | Observe-only; never intercepts the decision |\n\nBuilt-in anti-spam: per-agent per-kind throttle, 30s by default (`throttleSeconds`)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-notify\n```\n\nThe package declares `dsh.bundle`, so it **mounts itself on install** — no manual `insert` row needed. Just override the config by id in `~/.dsh/profiles/web/cordis.patch.yml` with your webhooks:\n\n```yaml\n- id: dsh-notify\n  config:\n    channels:\n      - type: wecom"
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```sh\nnpm install\nnpm test        # vitest, 16 cases\nnpm run build   # tsc → lib/\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Notes",
      "text": "- Webhook URLs are secrets — keep them out of public repos.\n- A failed notification only logs a warning; it never blocks the agent loop.\n- The plugin reads events and POSTs to webhooks only; message bodies contain just the agent label, tool name, and a truncated error summary — never your conversation content."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "[MIT](LICENSE)"
    }
  ],
